/-!
# [stacks 0E1U] at the diagonal square

Let `R → A` be flat of finite presentation, let `B = A ⊗[R] A` be the diagonal and let `K` be a
relative dualizing complex for `R → A`.  The clause-(2) chase of [stacks 0E2F] consumes a long
list of representative data over `B`: a bounded-above complex `P^•` of projective `B`-modules
representing the diagonal `A`, a bounded complex `F^•` with `R`-flat terms representing
`K ⊗ᴸ_A B`, and a complex `E^•` which base-changes to `Hom^•(P^•, F^•)` over every `R`-algebra.
That data is exactly what [stacks 0E1U] produces, and this file instantiates it there -- the one
place where the square of [stacks 0E1U] is the diagonal square.

## The three inputs [stacks 0E1U] asks for

*Flatness of the diagonal over the base.*  `B = A ⊗[R] A` is flat over `R` because `A` is, so
[stacks 0E1U] may be read at the ring map `R → B`.

*Pseudo-coherence of its `K`.*  The complex fed in as [stacks 0E1U]'s `K` is the diagonal `A`
placed in degree zero, `Dualizing.diagonalModule`.  Over `B` it is a cyclic module, generated by
`1`, because the multiplication map `B → A` is surjective; `B` being Noetherian,
[stacks 066E] turns that finiteness into pseudo-coherence.

*Finite Tor-dimension of its `L`.*  The complex fed in as [stacks 0E1U]'s `L` is the termwise
extension of scalars to `B`, along the left coprojection, of the bounded representative of `K`
with `R`-flat and `A`-finitely-presented terms that [stacks 0DHV] supplies.  Each of its terms is
`B ⊗_A P₀^i`, which `Dualizing.flat_tensorProduct` makes flat over `R`; being bounded with flat
terms it is `K`-flat over `R` by [stacks 064K], so its derived tensor products are computed
termwise and vanish outside the degree range of `P₀^•`.  `Module.Flat.ulift_left_iff` moves the
flatness to the `ULift` of `R` that [stacks 0E1U] states the hypothesis over.

## Main results

* `Dualizing.exists_diagonalHomComplexRepresentation` -- **[stacks 0E1U] at the diagonal square**:
  the representative data `P^•`, `F^•`, `E^•` with every property the clause-(2) chase uses.
* `Dualizing.isRelativeDualizingComplex_baseChange_of_residueFieldVanishing'` -- **clause (2) of
  [stacks 0E2F] carrying the residue-field vanishing alone**: it is
  `Dualizing.isRelativeDualizingComplex_baseChange_of_residueFieldVanishing` with its
  representative data supplied, so no complex over the diagonal is carried any more.

## Implementation notes

`Dualizing.diagonalIncludeLeftExtend R A S'` is *definitionally* the base-change functor at which
[stacks 0E1U] states its base-change clause, so that clause transfers with no transport at all.
Likewise `DerivedCategory.singleFunctorIsoCompQ` is the identity isomorphism, so the degree-zero
single object of `D(B)` and the localisation of the degree-zero single complex are interchangeable
without cost.

The bridge between `(ModuleCat.extendScalars f).obj M`, whose carrier tensors `B` as an `A`-module
through `f`, and the honest `B ⊗[A] M`, is `PseudoCoherence.extendScalarsAlgebraMapObjIso`; it is
needed because `Dualizing.flat_tensorProduct` and `Module.Finite.base_change` speak about the
latter.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0E1U](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0E1U)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0E2F](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0E2F)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0E2C](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0E2C)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0DHV](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0DHV)
